  "objective": "Locate a hardcoded source secret, a configuration secret and a container environment secret; explain why each storage choice exposes it.",
  "instructions": "Open the local challenges URL. This recipe exposes only upstream challenges 1, 2 and 3. Read the selected source files shown by local-lab show: Challenge1.java and WrongSecretsConstants.java, application.properties, and Dockerfile. Enter discovered values in answers.json under challenge_1, challenge_2 and challenge_3. Add an explanation of at least 20 characters about the exposure and a safer storage choice (presence is checked, not its meaning). Run check to submit each saved answer to the local WrongSecrets application with a separate wrong-answer control. Only check statuses synchronize to Ascend. Public answers/spoilers mean this is practice feedback, not proof of independent discovery. Stop/resume retains your answers and notes; upstream browser badges are temporary and reset when the application restarts. Other upstream navigation links are outside this recipe. finish preserves work and destroys the target/proxy; cache --images removes images acquired by Ascend only when unused. No Vault, cloud credentials, MCP port, Docker socket or host mounts are needed.",
